
<Defs xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="rimworld ../DefsSchema.xsd" xmlns="rimworld">

	<!--
		One line for every mamono corpse in the family: in the butcher menu, in
		stockpile and bill filters, and anywhere else that lists corpse categories.
		The insects, the slimes and the elementals all put their corpses here, so the
		player sees one "mamono corpses" heading instead of one entry per race.

		The def lives in this mod, not in a species mod, so every mamono mod can share
		the same line. Each species mod registers its own race defs with
		Source/ProjectMamono/MamonoCorpses.cs, and that file does the moving.

		Why this needs code (MamonoCorpses.cs):
		ThingDefGenerator_Corpses.GenerateCorpseDef picks a corpse's category with
		"race.Humanlike ? CorpsesHumanlike : race.FleshType.corpseCategory". The
		humanlike test comes first, so every mamono corpse - a humanlike race with its
		own flesh type - is filed with human corpses, whatever the flesh type says.
		There is no XML field for the category, and corpse defs are generated after
		XML patching, so no patch can reach them either.

		Child of CorpsesHumanlike on purpose, the way vanilla's CorpsesInsect is a
		child of CorpsesAnimal. That nesting is what keeps moving the corpses safe:
		anything already allowing humanlike corpses - the butcher bill, corpse
		stockpiles, the Ideology and Anomaly buildings that want one - keeps
		accepting a mamono corpse, and the filters simply show our line nested inside
		theirs.
	-->
	<ThingCategoryDef>
		<defName>PMM_MamonoCorpses</defName>
		<label>mamono corpses</label>
		<parent>CorpsesHumanlike</parent>
	</ThingCategoryDef>

</Defs>
